  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "| $t$ | $h(t)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $-5$ |\n| $0$ | $8$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ |\n| $4$ | $5$ |\n| $7$ | $-3$ |\n\nThe table above gives values of a function $h$ on the set $T=\\{-4,0,1,4,7\\}.$ Compute the following:\n\n${max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t)=$\n{{field-4}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-5,8,2,5,$ and $-3.$ The maximum output is $8$ (at $t=0$), and the minimum output is $-5$ (at $t=-4$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =8 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =0 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}h(t) & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
